    "full_description": "### Technical Specifications & Printing Guidelines\nThe official **Elegoo PETG + Carbon Fiber Composite** 1.75mm filament is engineered for high-performance 3D printing across FDM/FFF machines. Manufactured with strict laser-guided diameter control (±0.02mm), it delivers buttery-smooth extrusion without clogs or tangling.\n\n#### Key Features & Advantages:\n- **Combines**: Combines chemical resistance of PETG with structural stiffness of carbon fiber\n- **Heat**: Heat resistance up to 80°C and resistance to fuel, oils, and automotive fluids\n- **Outstanding**: Outstanding structural strength for drone arms and custom tooling\n- **Spool & Packaging:** Vacuum-sealed with industrial desiccant in heavy-duty moisture-barrier aluminum/poly bag.\n- **Universal Printer Compatibility:** 100% compatible with Bambu Lab (X1/P1P/P1S/A1), Creality (Ender, K1/K1C), Elegoo (Neptune 3/4), Prusa (MK3/MK4/XL), Anycubic, and Voron.\n\n#### Recommended Print Parameters:\n- **Nozzle Temperature:** 240 - 270 °C\n- **Heated Bed Temperature:** 75 - 85 °C\n- **Printing Speed:** 40 - 250 mm/s\n- **Cooling Fan:** 20 - 40%\n- **Build Surface:** Textured PEI, Smooth PEI, Glass, or Engineering Plate\n\n#### Available Color Options:\nStealth Black Carbon",
